; The normal p4gentmp2 systemd source sets rootcontext at tmpfs creation,
; before fd_reopen(O_DIRECTORY) checks read access. The raw executor SID, exact
; /run/credentials/<unit> path and ten literal units select one of these five
; root labels. Actual security.selinux readback is required before and after
; the original label_fix_full(); native mount/label failures have no fallback.
; No tmpfs context= override is used: children retain normal labeling. The
; original source seals the filesystem read-only before attaching it.
